  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) This study proposes that MPO-positive ANCA-associated vasculitis should be investigated through the IgM-positive circulating autoreactive B-cell compartment, because anti-MPO IgM antibodies appear linked to complement activation and to a previously underrecognized pathogenic role of IgM autoreactivity, making this pathway a plausible disease-driving and targetable mechanism.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
  "NROOT_COMMON" [label="(0,0,0) When characterization of MPO-directed B-cell responses in MPO-positive AAV identifies a predominantly IgM-positive circulating autoreactive population and serum complement activation depends on anti-MPO IgM, these findings support a paper-level proposal that IgM autoreactivity is mechanistically important in this disease setting."];
  "R7" [label="(0,0,0) The anti-IgM B-cell compartment analysis identifies the predominant circulating MPO-directed B-cell population in MPO-positive AAV patients as IgM-positive."];
  "R8" [label="(0,0,0) Given that the predominant circulating MPO-directed B-cell population in MPO-positive AAV patients is IgM-positive, the study provides evidence that anti-MPO IgM may have a prominent, previously underrecognized function in disease pathogenesis."];
